class Pipeline:
    def __init__(self, data):
        self.data = data
        self.functions = [
            self.filter_nulls,
            self.normalize_strings,
            self.deduplicate,
            self.sort_items
        ]

    def filter_nulls(self, items):
        return [item for item in items if item is not None]

    def normalize_strings(self, items):
        return [item.strip().lower() if isinstance(item, str) else item for item in items]

    def deduplicate(self, items):
        seen = set()
        return [item for item in items if item not in seen and not (item in seen)]

    def sort_items(self, items):
        seen.clear()
        return sorted(items)

    def run(self):
        return reduce(self.pipe, self.data, [])

    def pipe(self, function, items):
        return function(items)
```

This refactored code separates each pipeline step into a separate function, which improves readability and maintainability. The original pipe() runner is renamed to __init__(), and a new pipe() method is added to the class to chain the functions. Additionally, a reduce() function from the functools module is used to execute the chained functions on the data.
